-- the demonstration, computed and checked: for this molecule the bond graph predicts one proton signal
-- and the oriented molecule predicts two, and the two counts are not equal. Both numbers come out of the
-- same orbit computation over different groups — no rule of thumb, no drawing, and nothing read off a
-- string. Scaling this is a matter of supplying molecules and their automorphisms, which is what the
-- finiteness waiting on the-library-checks is for; the statement that the counts differ is here.
at-signal-counts-differ : chem-length At at-h-classes ≡ chem-length At at-or-h-classes → Empty
at-signal-counts-differ q = one-not-two (concat (sym at-h-signals-graph) (concat q at-h-signals-oriented))
